From: CloudAndX <cloudandx@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] allow the Android 16 KiB CPU on mach-virt

Patch 0011 registers the android-a57-16k QOM CPU type, but mach-virt also
checks every selected CPU against a separate hardcoded valid_cpus[] list.
Allow the registered Android-only model through that machine-level guard
without changing any existing CPU model or machine behavior.

diff --git a/hw/arm/virt.c b/hw/arm/virt.c
--- a/hw/arm/virt.c
+++ b/hw/arm/virt.c
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@ static const char *valid_cpus[] = {
     ARM_CPU_TYPE_NAME("cortex-a15"),
     ARM_CPU_TYPE_NAME("cortex-a53"),
     ARM_CPU_TYPE_NAME("cortex-a57"),
+    ARM_CPU_TYPE_NAME("android-a57-16k"),
     ARM_CPU_TYPE_NAME("host"),
     ARM_CPU_TYPE_NAME("max"),
 };
